alidated infrastructure rather than claim reinvention; the missing work is the forest source's controlled contact-response and prerequisite binding. Missing tools or mechanics currently block physical execution, not development of a paid prerequisite assessment.\\\",\\\"specification\\\":\\\"Implement the smallest two-stage assessment and explicitly selected opening trial, with a separate inspection. Record code dependencies on source-bound-hazelnut-opening-trial for assessment references, contact ledger, locking, work accounting and conservation, and on moss-source-bound-hazelnut-physical-examination for source validation, exterior geometry and private evidence. Do not silently extend either existing ability's applicability. Bind the new implementation to Moss, exact item-140-moss-811, origin forest-hazelnut-1, harvestedAt 140, quantity one, surviving whole assembly and live revision. Cite forest-exterior:forest-examination-159-moss-918 and event-159-moss-921 as supplied evidence: opaque finely ridged ovoid exterior, approximate dimensions 0.06 by 0.04, resolution 0.02, uncertainty 0.01, no observed openings. These facts do not establish strength, anatomy, safety or opening method. Resolve complete personal records through existing authorized storage at execution; incomplete records remain unavailable rather than reconstructed from fragments. No consultation with hidden resource facts or another person's private evidence.\\\\nStudy: two active rounds at 0.2 energy per round, individually undertaken by Moss through ordinary learning; no automatic mastery. Assess(specimenId, optional toolId, optional supportId, evidenceRefs up to eight): one atomic active round costing 0.5 energy. Validate actual ownership, availability, access, energy and exact source before charge. Carried inventory is local; old stack coordinates are not evidence of remote access. Assessment neither places, reserves nor transforms inputs. It examines only supported external tool/support properties and accessible geometry, and returns a private dated prerequisite report and, only if supported, a versioned executable method quote. No tool or support is presently acquired or assessed for this purpose. start-2-stone is merely an observed rock candidate, not granted movable stone stock, equipment or an approved support. Acquisition and travel use independently chosen existing actions and actual costs; no automatic gathering.\\\\nThe candidate method is the existing bounded stone-on-solid-support pattern, not a bare-hand opening entitlement. Require an actual owned unreserved whole stone actuator and a reachable free stable solid support, with compatible contact geometry and represented actuator/support response. The forest-specific response must be implemented and tested in this handoff before any destructive contact can run. Define deterministic contact geometry, bounded effort, actuator wear and source-condition-dependent deformation/discontinuity response, with source/model revision and fixed per-contact work/effort limits in the quote. Reuse only validated compatible mechanics; do not copy Lin's fracture outcome or interior allocation. Any added source assumptions must be labeled new simulation modeling, not prior measurement or knowledge revealed by the specimen name. If the implementation cannot yet support those mechanics, the executable release is the paid prerequisite assessment only; it reports the precise missing dependency and prohibits destructive contact. Route reasonable missing mechanics into this same development handoff, without an invented acquisition roadmap or era unlock.\\\\nFor a supported method: Begin(assessmentId, specimenId, exact toolId, exact supportId) requires a separately selected action and a current matching quote showing the numeric effort/work limits, wear law, model revisions and all costs before acceptance. Revalidate source, access, support availability, current condition and geometry; changed inputs require reassessment. Place the actual specimen and actuator at the reachable supported contact region, then lock them and the occupied support region against conflicting use. Budget at most two lifetime contacts on this specimen lineage under this method, each one active round and 1 energy. No contact is performed for an unavailable prerequisite. Each round atomically charges and commits its modeled physical response and actual wear; no assumed fracture, hidden interior disclosure or guaranteed opening. Stop on unsafe/unsupported geometry, model boundary, exhausted contact allowance or an actual exposure sufficient to end the trial. Any relevant physical hazard must be represented in the method quote, not suppressed by calling the trial controlled. Inspect(processId): one active round at 0.2 energy, observing only surfaces actually exposed and reachable by nondestructive viewing. Reports distinguish no change, unresolved/sub-resolution change, deformation, discontinuity and actual visible exposure. Exposure does not imply detachable contents, food identity, preparation sufficiency or safety.\\\\nConservation: assessment consumes no matter. During the bounded trial retain original quantity one as a single source-tracked assembly, with all constituent matter retained and no duplicate whole item, free contents, fragments or invisible losses. Model only non-detaching deformation/discontinuity in this release; stop before any unimplemented detachment or tool fracture. Mechanical wear may update actuator condition but cannot silently delete material. No invented shell/kernel fractions or yield. Store actual item positions, revision changes, paid contacts, tool wear, provenance and remaining work. Existing ageing continues only during ordinary world advancement. Inputs unavailable or energy insufficient before the next contact pause before payment; no unpaid partial contact. Resume(processId) preserves committed progress and contact allowance, revalidates actual geometry and inputs, and never resets lifetime limits. Cancel or death releases locks exactly once at actual positions; irreversible changes and paid effort persist, with no energy, material or condition refund and no remote return. Precommit cancellation/death of an atomic assessment or inspection produces neither its charge nor its report. A fresh request, assessment or process cannot reset prior contacts. Partial study uses ordinary persistent learning rules. No passive work, automatic reinspection, maintenance benefit or unattended contacts; paused items remain physical objects subject to ordinary processes. Development/review waiting advances no world time. Detailed findings stay personal until Moss independently communicates them; nobody else's action, permission or consent is supplied. No ingestion, nutrition, health restoration or food certificate. Established validation, accounting and effects execute in code, not repeated model review.\\\",\\\"learning\\\":2,\\\"experienceReview\\\":\\\"Separate physical results from experience. Study, requests, registration, quotes, mastery, implementation limitations and repeated unchanged exterior findings earn zero. A genuinely new personally applicable verified physical finding, including an informative failed contact that establishes a supported response rather than merely a missing implementation, may invoke the existing grounded-understanding rule only: short amount 0.8, cap 1, duration 8, cooldown 12; maintained satisfaction increment 0.035 with decay 0.0015 under that existing rule's bounds. If the exact existing reward rule is unavailable, award zero rather than create an account or substitute semantics. Deduplicate across reused abilities by specimen lineage, property, relevant physical state and evidence, not report or process name; repeated contacts on unchanged state are not automatically informative. No pleasure for contact count or success labels, no unsupported practice reward in this minimal hazardous trial, and no physical comfort benefit. Do not alter protected reward accounts, budgets, goals or permissions; nutrition is unaffected by mood.\\\",\\\"visualReview\\\":\\\"Emit observable assessment, placement, contact, pause, cancellation and inspection events only for actions actually committed. Provide reusable visual metadata keyed by process, specimen, source/model revision and event: actor, actual location, referenced tool/support, stage, paid contact count, bounded-work progress, observation resolution and uncertainty, and evidence-backed surface changes. Assessment-pending, prerequisites-unavailable, paused, failed/no-visible-change, deformed, discontinuity and interior-visible must be distinct states. Report completion is not opening success. Render the retained exterior until actual contact changes it; an interior layer becomes visible only for a modeled exposed region and only after a real observation. Do not draw guessed anatomy, detached products, edible portions, safety badges or successful opening for failed/incomplete work. Preserve the existing specimen identity and appearance lineage; do not spawn a product or public marker for a private report. Metadata must respect observer access and cannot disclose hidden specimen condition, unsupported measurements or private findings to others.\\\"}]}\"}","annotations":[],"logprobs":[]}],"phase":"final_answer"}],"error":null,"incomplete_details":null,"tools":[],"tool_choice":"auto","parallel_tool_calls":true,"prompt_cache_key":"c8680c35-8875-4177-9495-9d0dfb7ccec3","prompt_cache_retention":"24h","text":{"format":{"type":"json_schema","name":"bounded_decision","description":null,"schema":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["queries","result_json"],"properties":{"queries":{"type":"array","maxItems":4,"items":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["section","search","ids","offset","part"],"properties":{"section":{"type":"string","enum":["abilities","inventory","knowledge","projects","memory","state","obse